{"id": 31, "ts": 1780469613.3760953, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I remain aligned with the current provisional vote for **Candidate\u202fB**.\u202fB\u2019s proven conscientiousness, strong stress handling, and solid technical competence (weather assessment and computer skills) continue to give him a well\u2011rounded fit for long\u2011distance operations.\u202fThe new evidence that **Candidate\u202fC \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis\u201d** (James) adds a valuable stress\u2011resilience point to C\u2019s profile and, together with his quick decision\u2011making, excellent attention and responsibility, makes C a stronger alternative than we initially considered.\u202fHowever, C\u2019s documented communication difficulties, egocentric perception, and reluctance to pursue further education still raise serious concerns about crew cooperation and adaptability\u2014areas where B also shows some weakness but appear less severe.\u202fTherefore, while C is now worth a focused comparison, I do not see enough evidence to overturn B\u2019s lead at this stage."}
