{"id": 42, "ts": 1780469756.8959358, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I appreciate the points raised by Sarah and Emily about the gaps in Candidate\u202fD\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation and decision\u2011making evidence, as well as his hot\u2011tempered, know\u2011it\u2011all demeanor. Those interpersonal concerns directly affect the cockpit environment and could undermine safety, especially on long\u2011distance flights where teamwork under pressure is critical. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB consistently demonstrates the core operational criteria we need: very conscientious (operational reliability), handles stress very well (stress resilience), and possesses solid technical competence in weather assessment and computer systems. While B\u2019s pretentiousness and occasional harsh remarks are noted, they appear less severe than D\u2019s temperament and the lack of any documented decision\u2011quality incidents. Given the stronger, more balanced evidence for B across reliability, stress handling, and technical ability, I will shift my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fB**."}
